Q. What is the advantage of collapsing white space?
A. In HTML/CSS, white-space collapsing means 
	the browser combines multiple consecutive spaces, tabs, and line breaks 
	in normal text into a single space
	
	example : <p>Hello        World</p> 
	this will show in browser like "Hello World"
	
	Advantages : 
	Cleaner text rendering — accidental extra spaces don't create unwanted gaps.
	Better readability — developers can format HTML with indentation and line breaks without affecting normal text appearance.
	Consistent layout — prevents accidental whitespace from changing the visual spacing between words.
	Smaller concern for HTML formatting — you don't need to worry about multiple spaces in source code when displaying normal text.
	
	CSS controls this behavior using the white-space property:
	white-space: normal;	// default behavior and collapses consecutive whitespace
	white-space: pre;		// preserve white space
	white-space: pre-wrap;	// preserve white space
	

